      "id": "nebraska-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://nebraskalegislature.gov/laws/statutes.php?statute=25-2221",
      "title": "The holidays of Nebraska (Neb. Rev. Stat. § 25-2221, the days its courts may\nbe closed; § 62-301 lists the same days) that `us-federal-holidays` does not\nalready close: Arbor Day, the last Friday in April, and the day after\nThanksgiving. Both are always Fridays, so neither is moved off a weekend;\nthe section's other days are federal holidays observed on the federal\nschedule. The day after Thanksgiving is listed with `once` from the date the\nvendored text was retrieved (October 29, 2026; its edition is not dated) to\nthe end of 2050. Not modeled: days a specific court is closed by order of\nthe Chief Justice and the days declared holidays by law or proclamation of\nthe Governor, which no vendored source lists."
    }
